{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1s8YAozd67ubQiiG5je", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I've stopped before signing off. The device bridge has been down since about 12:21 (every call returns `BrokenPipeError`, including `observe`, `open_app` and `HOME`), and one finding is still unfiled.\n\n**Filed**\n- **Injection/Ampule strength label** (Add medicine): with Ampule selected the field reads \"Vial strength (mg)\" and switches to \"Concentration (mg/mL)\" when Vial is picked. The developer could not reproduce it from the steps I gave, so treat it as unconfirmed.\n\n**Not yet filed (reproduced once on screen)**\n- **Medication card caption in Edit group:** the Estradiol valerate card reads \"Injection · 5 mg\", but the Medicines list and Medicine details for the same medicine read \"Injection · Ampule · 5 mg\". This is the shared caption area in the build notes. I'll file it as soon as the device is back.\n\n**Unconfirmed**\n- The first time I saved a new Estradiol patch from Add group, the stock prompt showed \"0.120000005\", which looks like an unformatted float. I could not reproduce it, because that medicine now has stock tracking on.\n\n**Checked and behaving correctly**\n- Patch and Custom add-medicine validation (empty name, empty strength).\n- Cancel on the medicine edit sheet keeps the old value.\n- Body weight: 70 kg switches to 154.3 lb and the value persists; 0 shows \"Enter a valid weight.\"; Cancel on the Clear confirmation keeps the value.\n- Settings → First day of week set to Monday: it persists and the Plan week now starts on Monday.\n- Settings → Hide reference ranges: it hides the target range on Home.\n- Group rename persists; Archive removes a medicine from the list; the landscape rotation on Home is fine.\n\n**State I changed (test data)**\n- Estradiol patch 0.36 mg with stock tracking (8/8 patches) in group \"Morning\" (renamed from \"Group 1\").\n- Estradiol valerate tablet 1 mg; Estradiol Gel (Container, 0.3%, 80 g); Estradiol valerate Injection (Ampule, 5 mg).\n- Body weight 154.3 lb; First day of week Monday; Hide reference ranges on.\n- A \"TestMed\" tablet was created and then archived.\n\n**Not covered**\nSachet and Injection-Vial captions, the Calibration screen beyond a look, the Dose reminders toggle, and the App lock and Hide screen content toggles.\n\nI have not signed off, because the Edit-group caption finding is still unfiled and the rest of the Settings toggles and the Sachet/Vial captions are untested. Once the device tool is back, I'll file the caption report and finish those checks."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 882, "cache_read_input_tokens": 253283, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 882}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ff07104f-f854-4592-a09b-8cd3ab42a5b6", "uuid": "d0f4c48b-6205-4ce0-b457-a0a55219d6c2", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:21:51.340Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1s8XthmuJEcr37oNCa2"}
